WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:01.570
Nothing…happened…

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:02.570
- Scene Breakdown

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:04.610
What is the most iconic moment in all of One
Piece?

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:09.759
Now you yourself might or might not have a
specific answer to this question.

00:00:09.759 --> 00:00:14.320
However, whenever people ask me, “Hey Ohara,
what’s your favourite One Piece moment of

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:18.320
all time?”, there are always a bunch of
scenes and events that immediately come to

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:23.570
mind, but ultimately I can never decide which
one I like best.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:29.599
There is just so much greatness to choose
from, from very emotional stuff, over brilliant

00:00:29.599 --> 00:00:33.960
comedy, all the way to some of THE most badass
moments in anime.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:39.520
So, I thought to myself, if it’s so hard
for you to pick your favourite moment, why

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:45.520
not revisit some of them, find out WHY they
are great, and then pick a favourite.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:50.469
At first I was thinking about making this
a list video and simply presenting my top

00:00:50.469 --> 00:00:56.129
picks, but then I thought to myself that a
video “the top 10 most iconic One Piece

00:00:56.129 --> 00:01:00.789
moments” really doesn’t fit in well with
what we’re trying to do here on the channel.

00:01:00.789 --> 00:01:05.540
It also sounded like there were probably already
at least a thousand or so of these out there.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:10.810
And so I quickly scratched that idea and went
back to the drawing board and by drawing board

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:16.310
I mean I got a cup of coffee and watched some
anime, because I’m a goddamn genius when

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:18.310
it comes to procrastinating.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:22.520
But then I really sat down, and this time,
I fell asleep.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:27.369
I honestly was a bit discouraged whether I
would be able to pull this off somehow and

00:01:27.369 --> 00:01:32.170
was ready to simply ditch the idea and focus
my analysis videos.

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:34.840
After all, that’s what I’m actually good
at.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:39.090
And then it hit me: Why not do exactly that?

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:44.450
Why not analyse these scenes and see what
makes them tick, why they became so popular

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:48.560
and ultimately pick the most iconic moment
in One Piece.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:53.950
Apart from a couple of fight analyses, I don’t
think I’ve ever come across a proper scene-analysis

00:01:53.950 --> 00:02:00.969
for an anime; and so I welcome you to my new
format: The iconic scene analysis series…I

00:02:00.969 --> 00:02:04.020
think, we might have to work on that name
though.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:09.460
I’m super excited to try something new and
I hope that this format is something YOU will

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:10.460
enjoy as well.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:12.390
So, let’s give it a go.

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:17.540
To break down every scene, we will be looking
at things like theme, composition, framing,

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:23.570
body language, dialog, symbolism, music and
voice acting in the anime, the role the scene

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:27.830
plays for the overarching story line and much
, much more.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:32.250
And so, for the very first video in this series,
I thought it might be appropriate to start

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:36.850
with a banger right out of the gate, with
undoubtably one of my favourite moments in

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:43.450
the story and one of the best, if not maybe
THE best in Zoro’s arc: The Nothing happened

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:45.140
scene on Thriller Bark.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:50.230
The scene takes place shortly after the straw
hat’s united effort to defeat Moria and

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:57.870
his gigantous zombie Oars and stretches from
chapter 483 to chapter 486, and in the anime

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:03.810
it’s episode 377, in case you wanna follow
along.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:08.560
Luffy is knocked out from his intense final
battle and the rest of the crew, as well as

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:13.340
Lola and her men are resting after they finally
got their shadows back.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:18.170
However, right when they have defeated one
of the Shijibukai, Kuma suddenly appears on

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:19.170
the island.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:25.000
He had been tasked to inform Moria of Blackbeard
replacing Crocodile, of Ace having been captured

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:28.240
and of the potential conflict with the Whitebeard
pirates.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:33.820
However, upon reporting that Moria has been
defeated by Luffy, Kuma reeves new orders

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:39.500
to capture the crew and kill the remaining
witnesses, so no word of Moria’s defeat

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:43.940
can leak into the world to ruin their reputation
even further.

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:48.850
Kuma then compliments the unconscious Luffy
on the crew he has gathered, to which all

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:54.540
of the straw hats react in a hilariously flattered
way, despite the serious situation they’re

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:55.540
in.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:04:00.590
And despite the damage all of them took, Zoro
immediately prepares to fight Kuma to protect

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:05.630
his crew, and for the first time in this scene
mentioning his willingness to die fighting,

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:06.810
if necessary.

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:12.280
Kuma however easily repels each of Zoro’s
attacks and introduces his unique devil fruit

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:16.130
powers to the crew, that allows him to repel
anything.

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:21.450
As Kuma catches Zoro by surprise, Sanji jumps
in for the first time to help Zoro.

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:27.220
However, Kuma takes no damage from either
of the two and after proving his superiority,

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:32.350
he offers everyone present a surprising deal,
that goes against his orders.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:38.310
He will let everyone present on the island
live in exchange for Luffy’s life.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:42.910
Without so much as a second thought, all of
the straw hats as well as Lola and her men

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:46.090
refuse, and stand between Kuma and Luffy.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:51.750
As a result, Kuma takes out everyone gathered
there with an enormous shockwave and approaches

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.550
Luffy on his own.

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:58.730
However, before he reaches him Zoro, who seems
to be the last one standing, stands in his

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:00.340
way once again.

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:05.480
This time he manages to inflict damage to
the warlord, only to find out that he is indeed

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:10.680
a cyborg developed by doctor Vegapunk and
Kuma reveals the secret government project

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:12.790
of the pacifista.

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:18.410
Having witnessed Kuma’s true strength, Zoro
realises there is no way he can win this fight

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:23.940
in his condition and he bows down to offer
Kuma HIS life instead of Luffy’s, bargaining

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:26.980
his ambition to become the strongest swordsman.

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:32.020
Before Kuma can react however, Sanji , who
seems to be on the brink of loosing consciousness,

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:37.940
steps in, prepared to in turn give HIS life
to save both Zoro’s and Luffy’s dream.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:43.120
Zoro has made up his mind though, and acknowledging
Sanji’s gesture, he knocks him out with

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:44.310
his sword.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:47.520
Kuma then proposes another trial for Zoro.

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:52.740
Using the powers of his devil fruit, he expels
Luffy’s pain and fatigue and gives a portion

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:57.660
of it to Zoro, telling him that taking in
all of it would kill him.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:02.750
Zoro however, takes in all of Luffy’s pain
without a second thought.

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:07.490
Kuma then acknowledges Luffy’s crew and
leaves the island.

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:12.530
After regaining consciousness, Sanji hurries
to Zoro’s side finding him standing straight

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:14.610
in a puddle of blood.

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:20.590
Upon asking what in the world has happened
here, Zoro simply states that - nothing happened

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:24.300
- one of his most iconic lines in the series.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:30.200
A bit later, Luffy is shown miraculously back
at full strength, while Chopper states that

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:34.740
the now unconscious and treated Zoro only
closely escaped death.

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:40.290
Finally, Sanji stops two of Lola’s men sharing
what has happened, to not diminish Zoro’s

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:41.290
sacrifice.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:47.990
So, next to the obviously fantastic plot in
here, what makes this scene so damn good?

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:51.960
How did it become one if THE most memorable
moments for Zoro?

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:56.580
The first thing we should look at, is how
the scene fits in with the overall story and

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:58.400
what purpose it serves.

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:04.120
The epilogue scene with Kuma on thriller bark,
to me, seems to have four major implications

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:06.340
for the plot of One Piece.

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:10.000
First of all, it is of course meant to introduce
Kuma as a character into the story.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:16.210
While at the beginning of the scene Oda implies
him to be a cold and unforgiving government-loyalist,

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:20.670
hammered home by his epithet “the tyrant”,
over the course of events, it becomes clear

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:25.030
that Kuma is in fact sympathetic towards Luffy
and the crew.

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:29.480
Despite his orders and grim threats to take
Luffy’s head, he ends up letting everyone

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:31.400
on Thriller Bark walk away freely.

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:37.120
His affiliation with the revolutionaries is
also already hinted at here, when name-dropping

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:38.120
Dragon.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:43.420
And so, in just a few chapters, we get an
enormous amount of character development for

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:48.480
Kuma, that is still relevant until now, when
thinking about his role during the reverie-arc.

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:55.540
Secondly, the entire scene contains enormous
foreshadowing, for the next four arcs.

00:07:55.540 --> 00:08:00.889
Kuma is the first to mention Ace’s capture
by the marines and the upcoming conflict with

00:08:00.889 --> 00:08:05.630
Whitebeard, foreshadowing both the the events
at impel down and marine ford.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:10.060
At the same time, the introduction of his
powers and his combat superiority towards

00:08:10.060 --> 00:08:15.630
the crew heavily foreshadows the events at
Sabaody and finally the time skip, by indicating

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:20.460
that the crew is not strong enough to even
face all of the Shijibukai, let alone the

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:22.630
Marine admirals or the Yonko.

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:28.699
Thirdly, by testing their resolve, the entire
sequence serves as the ultimate proof of the

00:08:28.699 --> 00:08:34.080
straw hats’ loyalty towards Luffy, before
heading into the dark trilogy arc of defeat

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.080
for the crew.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:39.470
These three things aren’t as obvious when
reading or watching the scene itself, but

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:44.650
do a wonderful job as an underlying message
and vibe here, that really pays off in the

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:46.200
story going forward.

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:52.490
However, the last and undoubtably most impactful
purpose of this moment, is the characterisation

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:58.180
it gives to Sanji and especially to Zoro,
establishing both of them as Luffy’s left

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:03.550
and right hand and lifting Zoro up, to be
to Luffy, what Rayleigh was to Roger.

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:05.170
More than a crew-member.

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:06.589
More than a friend.

00:09:06.589 --> 00:09:12.730
More than a first mate, but a brother, standing
side by side with Luffy, a pillar for his

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:15.260
captain to lean and rely on.

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:20.990
It is some of the best characterisation in
the entire story and, even more than before,

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:26.339
Zoro’s sacrifice made him one of the most
respected and beloved characters of the series.

00:09:26.339 --> 00:09:31.570
So, now let’s dive a little bit into the
details here, and I’ll be referencing both

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:36.760
the manga and the anime here, both of witch
have done a fantastic job with this scene

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:40.710
and both of which have their innate bits that
they excel at here.

00:09:40.710 --> 00:09:45.680
What I think really stands out in this scene
in particular, even for anime and manga, is

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:49.410
the character’s body language and the fantastic
dialogue.

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:54.790
Kuma’s appearance switches between laid-back
and natural, such as sitting on the wall with

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:59.680
his legs crossed, reading his book and talking
on the den-den mushi - and at other times

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:02.820
moving and behaving mechanical and stiff.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:07.910
The same goes for his lines, that alternate
between robotic, very simple sentences and

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:12.950
words on the one hand, and quite eloquent
and intelligent lines on the other, that hint

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:15.560
at a smart and compassionate person.

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:22.110
Oda wonderfully uses every aspect of Kuma
to hint at the dichotomy as an intelligent

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:27.020
and friendly member of the revolutionary army
and the brainless, unforgiving machine following

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:32.080
the world government’s orders, switching
between human and machine.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:36.830
The straw hats meanwhile express nothing but
unity, loyalty and determination through their

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:39.940
body language and their dialog in this scene.

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:43.720
All of them see the danger they are in, and
yet all of them make it clear through their

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:49.339
words and general demena, that they will stand
by Luffy, no matter what.

00:10:49.339 --> 00:10:54.500
Especially Zoro and Sanji leave absolutely
no doubt that they see each other as Luffy’s

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:59.620
representation to protect the crew and uphold
his determined and unwavering will in his

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:00.620
stead.

00:11:00.620 --> 00:11:05.589
In more than just one scene, Zoro’s face
and the heavy breathing, included in his lines,

00:11:05.589 --> 00:11:10.520
hammer home the feeling that he is already
way beyond his last reserves of energy and

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:14.110
is mostly running on willpower and determination
alone.

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:19.610
Nonetheless, the look in his face when stepping
into the bubble of pain, suggests nothing

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:24.820
else than Zoro being fully prepared to die
here, without any regrets.

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:31.649
It is very powerful visual depiction of emotion
and motivation, that the manga does an especially

00:11:31.649 --> 00:11:33.190
amazing job with.

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:38.920
And I can’t even begin to describe how powerful
Zoro’s pose at the end is, covered in blood

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:40.890
and at the brink of death.

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:45.680
The anime meanwhile does a wonderful job in
terms of sound design and music in this scene.

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:51.100
The buildup to the climax is accompanied by
uneasy orchestral music, giving the scene

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:56.350
a threatening, cinematic and epic feel, and
once Sanji regains consciousness and hurries

00:11:56.350 --> 00:12:02.590
to find Zoro, there is no music at all, implying
something terrible has happened, only to hear

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:09.640
to hear the epic theme of the very strongest
play and seeing Zoro’s defiant face.

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:12.209
Absolute goosebump material.

00:12:12.209 --> 00:12:15.160
There is also a nice amount of symbolism in
this scene.

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:19.840
The most striking however, is without any
doubt Kuma removing all of Luffy’s pain

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:24.880
and fatigue and shaping it into an enormous
red bubble, making it visible to us and to

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:28.990
Zoro, what Luffy endues ever arc for his crews
sake.

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:34.320
At the same time, Zoro literally embracing
Luffy’s pain and taking it in, is a wonderful

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:37.840
symbol for the relationship he has with his
captain.

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:39.730
Beautifully executed.

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:43.070
The last thing I wanna look at, is the framing
in this scene.

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:48.230
All throughout the sequence, Kuma constantly
tower over everyone else, representing his

00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:51.529
superiority and the helplessness of the crew.

00:12:51.529 --> 00:12:55.550
He is literally and obstacle too big to overcome.

00:12:55.550 --> 00:13:01.560
This consistency in framing is only broken,
when Zoro offers his life to Kuma in Luffy’s

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:05.240
stead, which shows both of them at the same
level.

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:10.620
Through his words, Zoro has earned to look
eye-to-eye with Kuma and has passed his test

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:11.980
for the crew.

00:13:11.980 --> 00:13:17.130
Some other great compositional scene’s include
Sanji standing between Zoro and Kuma and Zoro

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:22.290
bowing down before Kuma to beg for Luffy’s
life, all of which create an even more emotional

00:13:22.290 --> 00:13:25.510
and impactful atmosphere than this moment
already carries.

00:13:25.510 --> 00:13:32.600
And ultimately, Zoro bleeding with his arms
crossed is shown from below his waist.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:37.649
After his sacrifice, Oda has given lifted
him to higher moral ground and given him the

00:13:37.649 --> 00:13:40.920
perspective, Kuma had throughout the scene.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:46.470
While each of the elements here, plot, dialog,
composition, etc. is beautiful crafted by

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:51.459
Oda, it is the sum of these elements that
together creates a moment that surpasses its

00:13:51.459 --> 00:13:52.769
individual parts.

00:13:52.769 --> 00:13:57.980
It’s creates one of the most emotional,
inspirational and suspenseful moments of the

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:02.580
series and it is a prime example of what makes
one piece so great.

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:06.560
If you made it to this point, please let me
know your thoughts are on this new format

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:07.950
and if you would like to keep it going.

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:08.950
Thanks guys.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:08.951
Peace.

